Track 1: Azimuth Error on a Wet Envelope
- Story & Context: When harbor master Ewan Ross dredged a waterlogged diplomatic mail sack from the freezing water beneath Pier 9, the salt had glued dozens of late courier dispatches into a solid block of pulp. Callum set the SP-1200 to loop the faint frequency beep of an approaching freighter while the twins blew an octave-down chanter growl to mimic the vessel's arrival, framing the heartbreak of unread ink. "You stamped the date, but the harbor swallowed every syllable," belts a sampled street singer over the swung, dust-caked Detroit chord progression, establishing the heavy sea-drag groove of the waterfront.
